Implemented Vercel Speed Insights for HTML project

## What was implemented:

Added Vercel Speed Insights tracking to all HTML pages in the portfolio site.

## Files Modified:

- `/index.html` - Added Speed Insights scripts to the main landing page
- `/elysium/index.html` - Added Speed Insights scripts to the Elysium project page
- `/play/index.html` - Added Speed Insights scripts to the Play page
- `/mile10/index.html` - Added Speed Insights scripts to the Mile 10 project page
- `/sketches/index.html` - Added Speed Insights scripts to the Sketches page
- `/c4d/index.html` - Added Speed Insights scripts to the Cinema 4D explorations page

## Implementation details:

Since this is a Vite-based HTML project (not a framework like React or Next.js), I followed the HTML implementation pattern from the Vercel Speed Insights documentation. 

Added the following two script tags before the closing `</body>` tag in all HTML files:

```html
<script>
  window.si = window.si || function () { (window.siq = window.siq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js"></script>
```

These scripts:
1. Initialize the Speed Insights tracking queue on the window object
2. Load the Speed Insights script from Vercel's CDN at `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js`

## Testing:

- ✅ Build completed successfully with `npm run build`
- ✅ Verified Speed Insights scripts are present in all built HTML files
- ✅ No errors or warnings during build process

## Next steps:

After deploying to Vercel:
1. The `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` route will be automatically available
2. Speed Insights will start collecting performance metrics from visitors
3. Data will be viewable in the Vercel dashboard under the "Speed Insights" tab

No package installation was needed for the HTML implementation as the scripts are loaded directly from Vercel's CDN.
